  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interactive-elements.html#the-dialog-element:dom-dialog-open\r\n\r\n> attribute DOMString returnValue;\r\n> void close\\(optional DOMString returnValue\\);\r\n\r\nThe return value is defined as a DOMString, but I have a use case in which I want to return an object (with a property for each input in the dialog). I could JSON encode it, but that seems wasteful at best, and it wouldn't work for, say, a dialog returning an array of files, or a canvas that the user's drawn on, or a Fetch promise.\r\nCould returnValue allow other types?",
